[Music]  Netflix's post-apocalyptic thriller bird  bugs was its final hits of 2018  but now the streamer has been hit with  serious backlash over some footage  featured in the flick bird bugs featured  plenty of terrifying scenes but the  sequence that has sparked the most  discussion wasn't fictional it was  footage from a real-life tragedy and  that flicks us refused to remove it from  the film it recently came to lights that  the film incorporated actual footage  from a 2013 fiery train crash in the  town of Lac Megantic in Quebec Canada  when an unattended 74 car freight train  transporting crude oil rolled downward  and derailed multiple tank cars exploded  and caught fire resulting in 47 deaths  several other individuals were reported  missing at the time and have since been  presumed dead path of luck Megantic  downtown area was destroyed and the  majority of the downtown buildings that  didn't collapse or catch fire in the  incident were destroyed due to  contamination the scene featuring  footage of the real-life disaster  happens early on in Byrd box and while  the filmmakers only use small bits of  the tragedy lack of Megantic residents  were quick to notice that the clips are  indeed from the deadly accidents Lac  Megantic Mayor Julie Morin told the  Canadian Broadcasting Corporation that  she and the townspeople hoped that  Netflix would remove the footage she  explained we find that it's really a  lack of respect to use these images as  fiction and entertainment it's hard  enough for us it's a sudden Cecilia's  images when they are used normally and  respectfully on the news  just imagine to have them used to  fiction as if they were invented Maureen  also noticed that the sci-fi series  travelers also on Netflix had utilized  footage on the Lac Megantic disaster one  of the producers of the show came  forward to apologize and explained that  the images use were sourced through the  stock footage website pond5 she added  that there was quote no intention to  dishonor the tragic events of 2013 in a  statement made to the Canadian  Broadcasting Corporation she said that a  team is working to replace the footage  it didn't take long for the people of  Cuba to stand up against Netflix for  utilizing the footage in Byrd box either  Kubek Culture Minister Natalie wah  penned a letter to Netflix his chief  executive officer Reed Hastings  slamming the company for its quote lack  of compassion empathy and solidarity  Netflix says public policy director  Corey Wright has since responded to the  Retton  Planes explaining that a video and  images won't be removed from bird box  according to Bloomberg Wright said in a  letter the use of stock footage is a  widespread and long-standing practice in  the film and television industry as a  result stock images are commonly used  within content on Netflix and on other  services this widespread use prevents us  from making the changes you request  unfinished content going forward we and  the broader industry can do better this  is now the second wave of controversy to  crash over Byrd box as a film stirred up  storms of contention when people began  participating in a dangerous social  media stunt known as the bird box  challenge in which fans would blindfold  themselves and attempt to drive cars  walk through traffic or move down steps  without getting hurt hopefully Netflix  can learn something from this and as a  company said do better moving forward  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite stuff are coming soon  subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]

